      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Because udon has a mechanism to detect analog triggers, it is possible to\nSince udon has a mechanism to sense analog triggers, we need to be able to use analog triggers with all controllers as udon operations.\n(OculusTouch's initial trigger assignment is to buttons, so gimmicks that require analog triggers don't work well.)\nWe need to make it so that only the avatar gesture operations are not analog triggered.\nTranslated with www.DeepL.com/Translator (free version)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-05-26T15:12:35.270Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Mapping animations for models hasn't been much fun due to the way that touch controllers handle animations, fist would be the best option for me but unfortunately, for some reason it allows for partial triggering, causing my Shape keys to act odd when using them. If i knew there weren't any avatars that relied on this feature i would say to just remove it but it would probably just be best to add a setting for it.",
